# ── FACT 5 (task #106) — BARE ENTITY NAME IN CALL-ARGUMENT POSITION ─────────
# One row per CALLEE: how many nominal-entity-shaped string literals it is
# handed as its FIRST argument, tree-wide, plus an md5-8 of the sorted roster.
# Derived, never hand-listed — re-derive with:
#   python3 tests/logos/key_identity_scan.py src/compiler include/logos/compiler \
#       --argscan-raw
# A NEW callee that starts taking a bare entity name is a NEW ROW and reds; this
# is what makes a future `struct_lit("Foo", …)` red at birth even though
# `struct_lit` holds ZERO such sites today and so has no row.
#
# ⚠ PRESENCE HERE IS A CENSUS, NOT AN ACCUSATION. `make_synth_struct` (42) is
# the #102 FIX: its literal is the KEY into `synth_owner_pkg_`, which is what
# supplies the package — the opposite of a bare lookup. `satisfies`/`add_impl`/
# `add_blanket`/`add_shape_auto_impl`/`trace_satisfies`/`add_auto_impl`/
# `add_negative`/`resolve` are trait_engine_test.cpp, a TEST harness. The rows
# that are open questions are the RESOLVERS — find_struct_by_name (2),
# find_enum_by_name (3), make_generic_struct (8), make_generic_enum (3),
# enum_lit (3), enum_lit_data (3), try_variant (4), try_prelude (3),
# try_prelude_variant (3), prelude_remap (4), remap (2) — and they are task #98's
# and #100's subject, not this round's.
